1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cavazos Garza, Israel.  ''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700'', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, page
2 CONC  134, #431 [V, fol. 124, v., no. 67].  ...  This protolocolo is the '''will of Captain Miguel de la Garza Falcón'''.  It states that this document was witnessed by Lt. Nicolás de la Garza, bears no signature of the writer, and is 
2 CONC '''dated 8 May 1694''' at the Hacienda de San Francisco, Monterrey.  It states that the author was '''born in Real de Mapimi, Nueva Viscaya''', and is '''to be buried in the Iglesia Parroquial (Franciscan Convent of San Andrés Chu
2 CONC rch now razed) in the burial place he has near the side door'''.  His parents Blas de la Garza and Beatriz Gonzáles, his wife Gertrudis de Renteria, her parents Sargento Mayor Jacinto García de Sepúlveda and Doña Clara de Renteria
2 CONC , and his children Jacinto, Juana, Julián, Leonor, Clara, Micaela, Antonio Miguel, María, Beatriz, Félix, Juan, Pablo, and Manuel are identified.  Further, Juana's husband Antonio Rodríguez, Micaela's husband Fernando Sánchez de Z
2 CONC amora, and María's husband Alférez Juan de Villarreal are cited.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''__________________________'''
