1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Beatriz Navarro''' was born about 1564
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #Alonso de Sosa Albornoz, about 1585
2 CONT #Bernabe de las Casas, about 1602
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz and Alonso had one child: 
2 CONT #Ana de Sosa Albornoz
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz and Bernabe de las Casas had five children:
2 CONT #Beatriz de las Casas
2 CONT #Juliana de las Casas
2 CONT #Maria de las Casas
2 CONT #Alferez Mayor Marcos de las Casas
2 CONT #Bernabe de las Casas
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz was the daughter of Juan Navarro and Maria Rodreguez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz was a member of the Juan de Oñate Expedition.  Beatriz and Bernabe de las Casas met in New Mexico, during its conquest by Juan de Oñate, and she married him after her first husband was murdered by a member of the 1598 New 
2 CONC Mexico Expedition.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Links ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/estrada.htm The Descendents of Don Alonso de Estrada]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Children of Beatriz Navarro Rodriguez and Bernabe De Las Casas are: 
2 CONT * +Maria De Las Navarro, b. 1604, d. 08 Dec 1684, Monterrey, Nueva Espana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Beatriz Navarro Rodriguez and Alonso Albornes Estrada are: 
2 CONT * +Ana De Sosa Albornoz, b. 1570, Asturias, Espana278, 278, d. date unknown, Nuevo Leon278, 278. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/m/a/r/Andres-J-Martnez-faras/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0487.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Notes for MARIA-BEATRIZ NAVARRO-RODRIGUEZ-CASTANO-SOSA: A.K.A. Beatriz de Navarro. Her first marriage was to Captain Alonso de Sosa Albornoz (Murdered in New Mexico). A daughter from this marriage was Dona Maria-Ana de Sosa Alborn
2 CONC oz Navarro who married General Alonso de Farias Trevino. Source: New Mexico's First Colonists, compiled and arranged by David H. Snow.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Her first marriage was to Captain Alonso de Sosa Albornoz (Murdered in New Mexico). A daughter from this marriage was Dona Maria-Ana de Sosa Albornoz Navarro who married General Alonso de Farias Treviño. See New Mexico's First Col
2 CONC onists, compiled and arranged by David H. Snow.
