2 CONT Birth:	1566 - Lepe, Andalucía, Corona de Castilla, España Death:	1634 - Saltillo, Nueva Extremadura, Reino de Nueva España Parents:	Marcos Alonso De Arcon (Nacida De Aracon), Costanza Alonso De Arcon (Nacida De Aracon) (nacida De 
2 CONC La Garza)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Monitor, McAllen, Texas; June 24, 2001; page 8E … “Sample Lineages: Marcos Alonso de la Garza” ... “Marcos Alonzo Garza is the forefather of many that carry the last names of Garza, de la Garza, Falcon and Treviño. What is kno
2 CONC wn about Captain Marcos Alonzo Garza is that he was the son of Marcos Alonzo and Constanza La Garza. He also went by the names Marcos Alonzo Garza y del Arcon, Marcos Alonzo Arza y del Arcon, Marcos Alonzo Arza y del Arcon, Marcos
2 CONC  Alonzo Garza del Alcon , and Marcos Alonzo. He was from Lepe, Huelva, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is estimated he was born about 1550, came to New Spain serving the military and married in 1585 to Juana de Treviño from a prominent Mexico City military family. His assignments took the family to Durango and Zacatecas where hi
2 CONC s duties were supervising the mining of silver and gold. His whole family ended up in Nuevo Leon in the time period between 1596 and 1603, after completion of his military career. The family of Marcos Alonzo is included in the lis
2 CONC t of the 12 original founding families of Monterrey N.L. Mexico, which was founded in 1596.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not known where the "del Arcon" or "del Alcon" part of the last name came from. However, this ending had an impact on his son, Blas, for he used as his last name, de la Garza-Falcon. (Alcon is the ancient form of the word Ha
2 CONC lcon, Falcon) At the time it was common to use wither paternal or maternal last names.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Marcos Alonzo Garza never again used the paternal last name of Alonzo. Instead his sons Francisco and Pedro used the last name of "de la Garza," Blas used the last name of "de la Garza-Falcon," and Diego, Alonzo, a
2 CONC nd Jose used their maternal last name "Treviño."
2 CONT
2 CONT As to why the last name Alonzo was totally abandoned by the family is a mystery, but it may have to do with the fact that Alonzo last name of Lepe, Huelva, Spain was associated with the Jews. Hernando Alonzo financed and aided Her
2 CONC nan Cortez in his actions. After the conquest of Mexico City, Hernando Alonzo, a well known Jew in the New World, was becoming too wealthy and powerful, and thus a threat. Hernando Alonzo was burned alive under orders of the Inqui
2 CONC sition. While no link has been established between Hernando Alonzo and Marcos Alonzo, the name may have been changed for protection.
2 CONT
2 CONT Only to add to the speculation is the fact that Marcos took his family to Monterrey where many other families with Jewish roots had settled. The Treviños which Marcos married into were known to be converts from Jews to Christians.
2 CONT
2 CONT Today many people go by the surname Garza having dropped the "de la" many years ago. There is also the surname Falcon having dropped the "de la Garza," de la Garza and Treviño, and all come from the same common ancestor. For more 
2 CONC information on this very topic refer to Tomas Mendirichaga Cueva's book "Origin of the Surname Garza and Treviño in Nuevo Leon". “
2 CONT
2 CONT YDNA Descendants of
2 CONT Capitan Marcos Alonso GARZA ARCON
2 CONT First 10 Generations
2 CONT
2 CONT by Crispin.Rendon
2 CONT
2 CONT There are over 114,000 descendants of Marcos Alonso Garza Arcon in our kindred database
2 CONT and of those over 3,700 carry his yDNA. Many but not all males with the surnames Falcon,
2 CONT Garza, Montemayor and Trevino are Y-DNA descendants of Marcos Alonso. The surname
2 CONT Garza Arcon is unique. Some have espoused that Garza Arcon should be Garza Falcon as used
2 CONT my Blas Garza Falcon. Three of Marcos' sons took their mother's surname Trevino (seen rarely
2 CONT as Temino). The surname Montemayor sprouts four generations later. This is a very different
2 CONT YDNA line then that of Diego Montemayor (founder of Monterrey) whose YDNA line died
2 CONT hundreds of years ago. Marcos Alonso's Y-DNA haplogroup is understood to be R-M269 and
2 CONT after Big Y DNA testing is now known as R-BY15969. Thanks to the efforts of David Reta and
2 CONT the FTDNA Garza DNA project for continued research with this ancestral line.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familytreedna.com/groups/garza/about
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally a word about the small town of Lepe, Spain where Marcos Alonso was born. When you
2 CONT tell someone from Spain that your ancestor was from Lepe they may smile expecting that you
2 CONT are joking, the reason being that Lepe is famous in Spain for being the subject of jokes.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Capitan Marcos Alonso GARZA ARCON, born in Lepe, Huelva, Spain, son of Marcos
2 CONT ALONSO. He married in Mexico City, D.F., Mexico.
2 CONT  Children of Capitan Marcos Alonso GARZA ARCON were as follows:
2 CONT + 2 i Capitan Alonso TREVINO, died Dec 1654 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT He married (1); (2); (3).
2 CONT + 3 ii Capitan Pedro GARZA, died 8 Feb 1639 in Salinas Victoria, Nuevo Leon,
2 CONT Mexico. He married (1); (2).
2 CONT + 4 iii Marcos Alonso GARZA, died Dec 1654. He married.
2 CONT + 5 iv Capitan Blas GARZA FALCON, died 21 Feb 1669 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon,
2 CONT Mexico, buried 21 Feb 1669 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico. He married.
2 CONT + 6 v Capitan Diego TREVINO. He married.
2 CONT + 7 vi Capitan Francisco GARZA. He married (1); (2).
2 CONT + 8 vii Caudillo Joseph TREVINO, died 12 Nov 1646 in Apodaca, Nuevo Leon,
2 CONT Mexico. He married (1); (2). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
