1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cavazos Garza, Israel.  ''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700'', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, page
2 CONC s 101-102, #348 [IV, fol. 110 v., no. 48].  ...  This protocolo is the '''will of Nicolás de Quintanilla''' and identifies his deceased parents Bartolomé González and Ana de Quintanilla, wife Beatriz Hernández (''sic''), wife's de
2 CONC ceased parents Capitán Gregorio Fernández and Beatriz González, his children, and some siblings.  It stipulates that he be buried in "la parochial" where his mother is buried.  Signed Monterrey, 13 January 1689.
