1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.currays.net/Gonzalez%20Web%20Project/ps03/ps03_417.htm  ...  Martha Duron Jimenez and Ignacio Narro Etchegaray.  ''DICCIONARIO BIOGRAFICO DE SALTILLO'', Mayo 1995, pages 157-158  ...  '''Diego SANCHEZ NA
2 CONC VARRO'''.  Native and citizen of Saltillo.  '''Son of Capitan Martin SANCHEZ Y SUAREZ de LONGORIA and Dona Melchora NAVARRO''', daughter of Capitan Juan NAVARRO and Maria RODRIGUEZ de SOSA.  His '''first wife was Maria de MORALES'
2 CONC '', daughter of Juan de MORALES and Isabel GUTIERREZ.  Their daughter, Melchora NAVARRO, married Juan GALINDO. Don Diego’s '''second wife was Feliciana BOTELLO''', daughter of Capitan Andres CAMACHO and Juana BOTELLO.  Their child
2 CONC ren were Bernabe, Juana, Diego, and Martin.  He raised a child from birth whom he named Juan SANCHEZ.  He engaged in agriculture and ranching.  He had a home in the Estancia de Santa Ana, jurisdiction of Saltillo, which he had inh
2 CONC erited from his parents.  His home in Saltillo was located on the plaza.  He made a will in Saltillo in November of 1670.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raul J. Guerra, Jr., Nadine M. Vasquez, Baldomero Vela, Jr.   ''INDEX TO THE MARRIAGE INVESTIGATIONS OF THE DIOCESE OF GUADALAJARA'', Vol. 2, 1997, page 347  ...   Genealogical Chart #13:  MARTIN SANCHEZ TREVINO + MELCHORA NAVARRO
2 CONC  RODRIGUEZ;  1. '''DIEGO SANCHEZ NAVARRO''' + (1) Maria de MORALES (MARTINEZ)
