2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coat_of_arms_of_Mexico  The coat of arms of Nuevo León]  is made up of four squares that form of a cross. Above, six bees represent the hard-working nature of local inhabitants. In the upper left sect
2 CONC ion is the Sun next to La Silla Hill and, in the foreground, an orange. In the upper right-hand square is a crowned lion ready to attack.  ...In the lower part of the coat of arms is the motto Sempre Ascendens, which means rising 
2 CONC up in search of the best. In 1582, the King of Spain, Felipe II, granted '''Luis Carvajal''' y de la Cueva authorization to colonize these lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.library.nd.edu/rarebooks/digital_projects/inquisition/collections/RBSC-INQ:COLLECTION/essays/RBSC-INQ:ESSAY_TrialsAndSentencing?genre_form_id=RBSC-INQ%3ATrials_and_sentencing  '''Introduction to inquisition trial trans
2 CONC cripts and records'''] . . . . In theory, all stages of a formal trial by inquisition should have been diligently recorded and carefully archived for future reference.  Countless folios of parchment and paper were undoubtedly fill
2 CONC ed by scribes from the very earliest days of inquisitorial activity; yet few early exemplars have survived. 
2 CONT
2 CONT . . . More or less complete trial transcripts have been identified, published and studied at length in many instances: 
2 CONT
2 CONT The spectacular cases of archbishop '''Carranza (1559-1576)''', cardinal '''Morone (1552-1559)''' or '''Galileo Galilei (1633)''' are well known, but even those of lesser figures such as''' the Mexican crypto-Jew Luis de Carvajal 
2 CONC and his family (1589-1596)''' have found their audience. 
