1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "'''México, bautismos''', 1560-1950," index, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.1.1/NY3Q-Z8W : accessed 26 Sep 2013), Ignacio De La Guerra, 06 Nov 1633.  ...  Name: '''Ignacio De La Guerra'''; Gender: 
2 CONC Male; '''Christening Date: 06 Nov 1633'''; Christening Place: '''Asunción Sagrario Metropolitano, Centro, Distrito Federal, Mexico'''; Father's Name: Antonio Guerra De Cañamal; Mother's Name: Luisa Hernandez Rio
2 CONT
2 CONT See a '''photograph of Ignacio's original Baptism Record''' in his profile's "Media/Documents" section.
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Ignacio has been listed as Escribano Publico de la Ciudad de Monterrey ( Public Scribe, Notary, Judge Secretary of the City of Monterrey).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ignacio Guerra Canamar was born in Mexico City on the 6th of November in the year of 1633. In his will, he listed his parents as Capitan Antonio Guerra Canamar and Dona Lucia Fernandez de Rio Frio. Ignacio married Maria de la Garz
2 CONC a, the daughter of Juan Cavazos and Elena de la Garza in his first marriage and Catarina Fernandez, the daughter of Capitan Gregorio Fernandez and Beatriz Gonzalez, in his second marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He listed children of the first marriage with Maria de la Garza as follows:
2 CONT * Elena Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Jose Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Juan Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Domingo Guerra Canamar - Priest  
2 CONT * Antonio Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Clara Guerra Canamar - also took the name as Clara de la Garza at times  
2 CONT * Ignacio Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Andres Guerra Canamar 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of the second marriage were as follows:
2 CONT * Cristobal Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Maria Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Francisca Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Luisa Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Clara Guerra Canamar - a second daughter named the same as one from first marriage  
2 CONT * Manuela Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Catalina Guerra Canamar  
2 CONT * Gregoria Guerra Canamar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ignacio's will was either written or entered into the Protocolos de Monterrey on the 20th of November of 1701 and it was recorded that he died on 7th of December of 1701 in Cerralvo. He was 68 years of age when he died. The will s
2 CONC tated that he wanted to be buried in a humble spot of the Convento de San Francisco.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hispanicgs.com/igg.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Ignacio GUERRA934 was born (date unknown). Parents: Antonio GUERRA and Luisa FERNANDEZ.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Maria CAVAZOS (aka Maria de la Garza). Maria CAVAZOS (aka Maria de la Garza) and Capt. Ignacio GUERRA were married. Children were: Capt. Andres GUERRA, Capt. Juan GUERRA, Capt. Ignacio GUERRA, Capt. Joseph GUERRA, Clara GU
2 CONC ERRA, Antonio GUERRA.
2 CONT
