1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Maria Zapata''' born c. 1674 died December 4, 1761, age 87
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Diego-de-Medina/6000000001500800498 Diego de Medina]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Maria Zapata and Diego de Medina:
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Ramon-Medina/6000000001500764145?through=6000000013126624193 Ramon de Medina]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Juana-de-Medina/6000000001500764096 Juana de Medina]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Isidro-Medina/6000000001500764113 Isidro de Medina]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Rosa-Medina/6000000001500764121?through=6000000001500764113 Rosa de Medina]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Lugarda-Madina/6000000001500738995?through=6000000001500764121 Lugarda de Medina]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Diego-de-Medina/6000000001500743893 Diego de Medina]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Josefa-de-Medina/6000000013129739331 Maria Josefa de Medina]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Antonia-Medina/6000000001500764088?through=6000000013129739331 Antonia Catarina de Medina]
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Zapata is the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Captain-Jos%C3%A9-T%C3%A9llez-Gir%C3%B3n/6000000008019959205?through=6000000008019915347 Captain José Téllez Girón] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Catalina-Romero/600000
2 CONC 0008019915347 Catalina Romero]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT She appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth household, five daughters, five dependents
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain José Téllez Girón, married to doña Catalina Romero, with one daughter named Jacinta Téllez Girón and another named '''Maria Zapata'''.  He states that he has a daughter, a young woman named Juana José Téllez, with his brot
2 CONC her, Juan Téllez Girón.  She writes to his son to bring her.  He also states that he has two other children, Lucia and Catalina, and five dependents, named Gertrudis, Maria, Josefa, and Isabel, and Nicolas.  As a loyal vassal of h
2 CONC is majesty, he is quite ready to enter whenever I, the governor and captain general, enter to settle this kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
