1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cavazos Garza, Israel.  ''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700'', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, page
2 CONC  134, #431 [V, fol. 124, v., no. 67].  ...  This protolocolo is the '''will of Captain Miguel de la Garza Falcón'''.  It states that this document was witnessed by Lt. Nicolás de la Garza, bears no signature of the writer, and is 
2 CONC '''dated 8 May 1694''' at the Hacienda de San Francisco, Monterrey.  It states that the author is '''to be buried in the Iglesia Parroquial (now the Monterrey Cathedral) in the burial place he has near the side door'''.  His paren
2 CONC ts Blas de la Garza and Beatriz Gonzáles, his wife Gertrudis de Renteria, her parents Sargento Mayor Jacinto García de Sepúlveda and Doña Clara de Renteria, and '''his children''' Jacinto, Juana, Julián, Leonor, Clara, Micaela, An
2 CONC tonio Miguel, María, Beatriz, Félix, Juan, Pablo, and Manuel are identified.  Further, Juana's husband Antonio Rodríguez, Micaela's husband Fernando Sánchez de Zamora, and '''María's husband Alférez Juan de Villarreal''' are cited
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista de VILLARREAL1175 was born (date unknown). Parents: Capt. Juan Bautista de VILLARREAL and Luisa DE LA GARZA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Gregoria DE LA GARZA. Gregoria DE LA GARZA and Juan Bautista de VILLARREAL were married on 8 August 1695.1234 The marriage investigation by the Church was done on February 15, 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b239.html#P7561
