1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Diego de HINOJOSA836,2146 was born about 1630.2147 He died in 1673 at the age of 43.2146,2147 He was killed by Indians in the Rio Blanco area, in the valley of San Antonio de los Llanos (now Hidalgo, Tamaulipas). P
2 CONC arents: Vitali de HINOJOSA and Maria MONTANO.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Maria CANTU. Maria CANTU and Diego de HINOJOSA were married. Children were: Juliana de HINOJOSA, Maria de HINOJOSA, Miguel de HINOJOSA Montano, Clara de HINOJOSA, Diego de HINOJOSA.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b117.html#P7472
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died in San Antonio, De Los Llanos, Nuevo Leon, Mexico
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego Hinojosa Montano was killed by an Indian that  fooled him by carrying a large religious cross,
2 CONT He was in a fort with other colonists and he thought the Indian wanted peace since he was showing the big cross.
2 CONT No sooner was Diego de Hinijosa Montano out the gates when an arrow pierced his heart,, \
2 CONT I found this information on a book of the Last names  of Nuevo Reino de Leon, Tamaulipas, Coahuila and Texas,
