2 CONC s 100-101, #348 [IV, fol. 110 v., no. 48].  ...  This protocolo is the '''will of Captain Pedro de la Garza''', born in Nuevo Leon and the '''son of Captain Pedro de la Garza and Inés Rodríguez''', both deceased.  He states that h
2 CONC e wishes to be buried in the Parrish Church and that he is '''married to María de la Rocha''' who had no dowry.  Their '''children are José (deceased), Pedro, María, Juana, Lucía, Nicolasa, Inés, Antonia, Francisco, and Juan'''.  
2 CONC He names his children's spouses and sets forth his debts and his bequests.  Dated 19 October 1688, Hacienda of Saint Nicolas, jurisdiction of Monterrey.
